{"title":"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On the graph chart, if the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/4/ad4c2f8ed306f3f2e193eeec9b6ab019631b56b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+5x+24=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e334b717aada139bb80069226d0d24b65c41c542.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+x+4=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" /> were graphed, at which point would they intersect?\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:1963_Algebra_I_22.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/c/c3/1963_Algebra_I_22.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"297\" height=\"296\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/7/7f7bba0435e4511d3d1e483081371da5f7b9d3b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)} \\quad A \\quad \\text{(B)} \\quad B \\quad \\text{(C)} \\quad D \\quad \\text{(D)} \\quad E \\quad \\text{(E)} \\quad F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"346\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In slope-intercept form, we have two lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/9/229b864fa2b1d4dcc71a151e9fdd453bfae6d324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-5x-24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb2eca8129ea3962761dd0f28ed3d05443507361.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-x-4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" /> Setting them equal to each other, we get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/46357bc8924cb5d1cdcfd1f84cc48ff1394d821d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-5x-24=-x-4 \\rightarrow \\boxed{x=-5}.\\]\" width=\"253\" height=\"25\" /> The only point with an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/2/a526e44e36254c196af103613bc724f312b6a209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/f/35f601621caef43cc3d45b70f24c69b3038d5c44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(C)} \\quad D.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"73\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Mathematics_Contests\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Mathematics Contests\">1963 TMTA High School Mathematics Contests</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems\">Problems</a>)</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_22\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problem 22\"> Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"40%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=TMTA_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_Past_Problems/Solutions\" title=\"TMTA High School Mathematics Contest Past Problems/Solutions\">TMTA High School Mathematics Contest Past Problems/Solutions</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problem_24\" title=\"1963 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018041546\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.026 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 75/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 661/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 305/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1732/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.565      1 Template:Succession_box\n100.00%    6.565      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20667:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018041546 and revision id 144623. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}